# November 21, 2026: region troy (Troy & Lansingburgh), drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny. Troy is the most
# worked ground in the state, so this batch takes what three earlier Troy batches left: the RPI hill (the 1907 Approach
# stair, the 1933 chapel that became the Voorhees Computing Center, and four campus buildings of 1906-1931), three former
# churches downtown and in South Troy (Woodside, the old First Presbyterian that is now Russell Sage's Bush Memorial
# Center, and the 1846 First Baptist church), Public School No. 1, and four places in old Lansingburgh from the 2023
# Central Lansingburgh Historic District nomination (two 1770s gambrel houses, the 1870 Fox steamer firehouse and the
# walls left of the Powers Opera House).
# Sources opened in this session: the RPI Institute Archives building histories (archives.rpi.edu), RPI News, HMdb
# marker pages, Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py), the National Register forms for Public School No. 1 and the
# Central Lansingburgh Historic District (NPGallery PDFs read with tools/page.py), the Lansingburgh Historical Society's
# Powers Opera House page, Baptist News Global and Atlas Obscura, all through tools/page.py; positions from the ArcGIS
# geocoder (tools/geo.py) and OpenStreetMap (tools/nom.py, osmnear.py).
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
